    {
      "id": "w2-title",
      "name": "Title Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Budget Coach Demo | WF2 — Scheduled Check-ins\n\nEntry workflow for everything the Budget Coach demo starts on its own. No Telegram trigger here: 5 schedule triggers (Europe/Rome) each build a synthetic message and call an agent (agents/ subfolder, locked to \"WF1\" and to this workflow). The answer goes to the service \"Budget Coach Demo | Send And Log Reply\".\nSections: Renewal Check (\"Subscription Agent\"), Budget Check-ins (\"Family Budget Coach\"), Month Setup (inline, creates the month's Budget Lines), Shared: All Sections (the send-and-log call).\nAll schedules switch on and off together (disable one schedule node to pause just one). Errors: \"Error Handling | Main — Error Handler\".",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 1800,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "w2-b",
      "name": "Renewal Check Section Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        528
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Renewal Check (\"Subscription Agent\")\n\nTriggered by: a schedule, every 2 days at 09:00.\n\nWhat it does: Tag Renewal Check sets mode = renewal_check and Call Subscription Agent runs the agent, which asks Notion for subscriptions whose \"Needs Alert\" is true. None: the run ends empty and nothing is sent. Some: one alert is written and sent.",
        "height": 580,
        "width": 1800,
        "color": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "w2-c",
      "name": "Budget Check-ins Section Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        1168
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Budget Check-ins (\"Family Budget Coach\")\n\nTriggered by: 3 schedules (Europe/Rome): daily 19:15 to Alex and to Sam, one message each (One Per Chat splits the two chats; skipped for a chat that already has a Budget Coach exchange logged today), Sunday 19:30 weekly summary, and the 1st at 08:00 month-end review of the month just closed.\n\nAll three build a synthetic message and call Call Family Budget Coach. Automatic messages are propose-only: nothing is written until you reply.",
        "height": 960,
        "width": 1800
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "w2-d",
      "name": "Month Setup Section Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        2192
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Month Setup (1st 06:00)\n\nTriggered by: a schedule on the 1st of the month at 06:00 (no AI).\n\nWhat it does: reads the Budget Categories and the Budget Lines, creates this month's missing Budget Line for every category with a default budget, and creates the month's Overall line from the previous month's cap (a cap set in euros is copied in euros too, and the Budget Coach converts it at the current rate). If it created anything it sends one confirmation line. It is logged as agent \"month_setup\" so it does not suppress the 19:15 check-in.",
        "height": 580,
        "width": 1800,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "w2-shared",
      "name": "Shared: All Sections",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1872,
        528
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Shared: All Sections\n\nReached after any agent call above returns, and after Month Setup.\n\nIf an agent call fails or times out, its error output goes to Build Check-in Error Reply: a chat message saying which agent could not send the scheduled message, why, and \"try again\" with the tag line (the alert comes from the agent's own workflow).\n\nCall Send And Log Reply runs the service that formats the reply for Telegram, logs it in the Agent Log and sends it (the same service \"WF1\" uses).",
        "height": 2240,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "set-checkin-error-reply",
      "name": "Build Check-in Error Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.5,
      "position": [
        1984,
        1216
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "e1",
              "name": "error_reason",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ /time(d)? ?out/i.test(JSON.stringify($json.error || '')) ? 'it timed out' : ('it failed: ' + String(typeof $json.error === 'object' ? ($json.error.message || JSON.stringify($json.error)) : ($json.error || 'unknown error')).slice(0, 200)) }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "e2",
              "name": "output",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "=⚠️ The {{ $json.agent_name }} agent could not send this scheduled message: {{ /time(d)? ?out/i.test(JSON.stringify($json.error || '')) ? 'it timed out' : ('it failed: ' + String(typeof $json.error === 'object' ? ($json.error.message || JSON.stringify($json.error)) : ($json.error || 'unknown error')).slice(0, 200)) }}.\n\nReply \"try again\" and I run it now.\n\n➡️ #{{ $json.agent_name }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "includeOtherFields": true,
        "options": {}
      }
    },
